      "message": "fix(ui): one work-turn display frame, fixed steel stays fixed (#4266)\n\nThe review of PR #4277 (head 8751fc52a) named four findings.\n\n1. Membership: the scene transform now turns only the steel that\n   turns with the work - the part, the stock and the fixtures whose\n   FixtureDef.fixed is false (`work_turn::turns_with_work`, the same\n   split `fixture::workholding_for` judges). A fixture declared fixed\n   stays in the machine frame; the tool body keeps its own pose.\n2. One display frame: the playback marker rides the carried tip\n   (`shell::sim_marker_pose`, the same pose the tool body draws\n   from), and the cached toolpath lines read turned through the same\n   turn as the models and the ground shadow (the shadow is now built\n   from the turned bodies). Machine-side elements stay fixed.\n3. Frame cost: the turned vertices, the turned path lines and the\n   turned fills are cached under their actual inputs - the source's\n   allocation identity, its length, its end probes and the work\n   turn's bit pattern (`frame_cache::TurnedCache`; the kept region's\n   fill id from `frame_memo`, never a document counter). A paused\n   playhead computes nothing again; a scrubbed turn rebuilds.\n4. Placement: `sim_machine_view` moves to camcraft-sim as\n   `machine_view` (pure vector/angle math, no document concern); app\n   re-exports it for the UI.\n\nTested: machine_view unit tests, ui lib scene tests\n(sim_work_turn, work_turn_tests), frame_cache counter pins.\n\nRefs #4266",
